# Rule: `.vercelignore` (wildcard + allowlist)

This repository is linked to a Vercel project with **Password Protection**.
Published paths are controlled by an allowlist in [.vercelignore](mdc:.vercelignore):
the first non-comment line is `/*` (ignores everything), and each `!path`
block opts a file or folder back in.

## Absolute rules

- **Never remove the `/*` line** in `.vercelignore`. Without it, the whole
  repo (including `.claude/`, `.cursor/`, `.vtex/`, source code, internal
  docs) would be served by Vercel by direct path.
- **Never replace `/*` with narrower patterns** (e.g. `/docs`, `*.md`). The
  wildcard is intentionally broad.
- **Never add patterns that re-include the whole repo** (e.g. `!*`, `!/`,
  `!**/*`).

## What you can do

- Add a `!path` block to publish a folder or file. Ask the user which
  subproject this is for before adding.
- Remove an existing `!path` block to take that path off the air.

**Ordering is significant.** `.gitignore` matching is order-sensitive (the
last pattern that matches wins). Inside a chained re-include block, do not
reorder the `!path` and `path/*` lines. Append new blocks at the end of the
file under a clear comment header.

## Nested paths require chained re-includes

Template for `modules/X/Y/prototype/`:

```
!modules
modules/*
!modules/X
modules/X/*
!modules/X/Y
modules/X/Y/*
!modules/X/Y/prototype
!modules/X/Y/prototype/**
```

Reuse intermediate directories that are already unblocked earlier; do not
duplicate. Always add a comment header naming the prototype being published.

More context in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md), [CLAUDE.md](mdc:CLAUDE.md) and
[.claude/vercelignore.md](mdc:.claude/vercelignore.md).
